{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879480",
      "title": "Using Custom CSS Class Names",
      "lectureOrder": 200,
      "videoOrder": 175,
      "sourceHash": "8a72149c9fc8324b6cc51bfe4f61ddae34a80c11c5eb0b5e383e038006297ed0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.1,
          "en": "Now what if you had",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.1,
          "end": 5.53,
          "en": "multiple transition components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.53,
          "end": 7.1,
          "en": "on your page though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.1,
          "end": 11.12,
          "en": "Because maybe you don't just want to animate the removal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.12,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "and addition of this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 16.643,
          "en": "but also off this div or of any other element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.89,
          "end": 21.88,
          "en": "Theoretically, that works, but you will face a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.88,
          "end": 26.63,
          "en": "Vue always adds the same CSS classes to all elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.63,
          "end": 29.44,
          "en": "which basically means you will use the same animations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.44,
          "end": 32.39,
          "en": "and transitions for all elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.39,
          "end": 34.05,
          "en": "Maybe that is your requirement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.05,
          "end": 35.47,
          "en": "Maybe that is what you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.47,
          "end": 37.58,
          "en": "but maybe you want different transitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.58,
          "end": 40.66,
          "en": "for different transition components on your page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.66,
          "end": 44.2,
          "en": "And that's why you can customize those names here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.2,
          "end": 48.21,
          "en": "We could, for example name this para-enter-from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 51.88,
          "en": "para-enter-active, para-enter-two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.88,
          "end": 53.89,
          "en": "and the same for the leave classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.89,
          "end": 57.56,
          "en": "instead of the v- thing at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.56,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "But with that Vue of course wouldn't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 65.21,
          "en": "that these are the CSS classes it should add and analyze",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.21,
          "end": 68.46000000000001,
          "en": "instead with just the names changed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 72.51,
          "en": "we have no animation because Vue will stick to its default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.51,
          "end": 76.65299999999999,
          "en": "v-enter-from, v-enter-to and so on class names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.95,
          "end": 82.43,
          "en": "We need to tell Vue that for this transition component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.43,
          "end": 85.64,
          "en": "it should add the para-classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.64,
          "end": 88.24,
          "en": "and we do so by adding a special name prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.24,
          "end": 89.72,
          "en": "to the transition component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.72,
          "end": 93.78999999999999,
          "en": "Here you add your custom prefix, which in my case is para,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.78999999999999,
          "end": 95.733,
          "en": "but which can be anything you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.97,
          "end": 98.32,
          "en": "And if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.32,
          "end": 102.63,
          "en": "now these para-enter-from, enter-active, enter-to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.63,
          "end": 106.55,
          "en": "And so on classes will be added and managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.55,
          "end": 108.533,
          "en": "and analyzed by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 112.99000000000001,
          "en": "So now with that, if you reload the animation is back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.99000000000001,
          "end": 116.47,
          "en": "So this name can be set and customized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.47,
          "end": 119.667,
          "en": "so that you can have multiple different transitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.667,
          "end": 123.37,
          "en": "and transition component usages most importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.37,
          "end": 125.033,
          "en": "in the same component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.95,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "Now, one more word about the naming here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 131.54,
          "en": "You can define your own custom prefix,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.54,
          "end": 134.72,
          "en": "as I explained here with the name prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.72,
          "end": 139.1,
          "en": "in cases where you wanna replace the entire class names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.1,
          "end": 143.47,
          "en": "So you don't wanna work with para-enter-from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.47,
          "end": 146.27,
          "en": "para-enter-active, para-enter-to and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.27,
          "end": 150.04,
          "en": "but you wanna use totally custom CSS class names here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.04,
          "end": 153.21,
          "en": "for example, because you're using some third parties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.21,
          "end": 155.09,
          "en": "CSS animation library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.09,
          "end": 158.09,
          "en": "which gives you certain classes you need to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.09,
          "end": 160.48,
          "en": "where you can't change the names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.48,
          "end": 165.4,
          "en": "For such cases, you can add more props here instead of name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.4,
          "end": 169.51,
          "en": "you can add, enter-to-class prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.51,
          "end": 173.53,
          "en": "and define your enter-to-class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.53,
          "end": 177.26,
          "en": "enter-active-class prop and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.26,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "So here you can, then define your CSS class names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 184.42,
          "en": "that should be added during the enter-to phase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.42,
          "end": 188.17,
          "en": "the enter-active phase and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.17,
          "end": 192.32,
          "en": "So instead of v-enter-to or para-enter-to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.32,
          "end": 195.82,
          "en": "you would then add some class and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.82,
          "end": 197.75,
          "en": "Now that's not what I'm doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.75,
          "end": 200.57999999999998,
          "en": "I'll revert this to name equal para,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 202.46,
          "en": "but I want to make you aware of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.46,
          "end": 205.32999999999998,
          "en": "so that you know that you have full flexibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.32999999999998,
          "end": 206.89,
          "en": "when it comes to these names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.89,
          "end": 209.82999999999998,
          "en": "And when it comes to which CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.82999999999998,
          "end": 211.913,
          "en": "are added at which point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
